# Dye Essence parameters (docs/specs/dye-essence.md §7). The order is permanent once a phase merges:
# songs and presets store values by position. New parameters go at the end; an enum's maximum may
# grow, its values never move. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/DyeEssence
namespace NeoBuzz.DyeEssence
class DyeEssenceMachine
tracks 16
summary Hybrid wavetable synth: three engine slots, each a morphing wavetable or an analog oscillator with 1–16 unison voices and two warps (bend, sync, FM, PM, AM, ring and more), a sub and a noise, samples (looped, reversed, tuned by root), granular clouds of them and additive partials (up to 128, morphing between sets, tilt, odd/even, stretch, damp), two filters per note (ladder, state-variable, comb; serial to parallel), oversampled 2× or 4×; two modulation envelopes, four LFOs (built-in or drawn shapes), four macros and sixteen routes. Use it for wide unison leads, evolving pads, FM and sync basses, plucks and bells.
import wavetable .wav | A WAV wavetable: frames of 2048 samples (or a clm chunk saying the frame size), or one short single cycle. Becomes a slot's "User" table: item 0 is slot A, 1 slot B, 2 slot C. The Harmonic engine reads its partial levels: the first frame is the "User" set, the last the "User" second set.
import lfo_shape .txt | A drawn LFO shape: a text file of breakpoints "phase,value[,curve]" separated by spaces (phase 0–1 across one cycle, value −1–1, curve −1–1: 0 straight, below 0 a fast start, above a slow one; a point at 0 and one at 1 make a jump at the wrap). item 0–3 picks LFO 1–4; its shape is set to Drawn.

import sample .wav | A WAV sample (mono or stereo, up to 20 s, kept in the machine state). Becomes a slot's "User" sample and sets that slot to the Sample engine (unless it is Granular): item 0 is slot A, 1 slot B, 2 slot C. The Sample and Granular engines play it; "A position" is where playback starts (Sample) or where grains are taken from (Granular).

group Voice
VoiceMode   "Voice mode"    0 2    0    enum Poly Mono Legato           | Poly; Mono retriggers; Legato glides without retriggering
Polyphony   "Polyphony"     1 32   8    int 0                           | Notes that sound at once
GlideMode   "Glide mode"    0 2    0    enum Off Always Legato          | When notes glide
Glide       "Glide"         0 1000 200  pow 0 2 3 s 3                   | Glide time
BendRange   "Bend range"    0 24   2    int 0 st                        | Pitch bend range
Quality     "Quality"       0 1    0    enum Standard_2× High_4×        | Voices at 2× or 4× the sample rate: High keeps hard FM, PM and sync cleaner at twice the CPU
VelAmp      "Vel → amp"     0 1000 700  pct                             | How much velocity changes loudness
Volume      "Volume"        0 1000 739  db -40 6 inf                    | Output level

group Osc A
AType      "A engine"      0 5    1    enum Off Wavetable Analog Sample Granular Harmonic | What slot A plays: a morphing wavetable, an analog wave, a sample, grains of a sample, or additive partials (samples, grains and partials take no warps)
ATable     "A table"       0 10   0    enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User | Wavetable (User: a table loaded for this slot)
APos       "A position"    0 1000 667  pct                             | Position in the table (frames morph smoothly)
AOct       "A octave"      0 8    4    int -4 oct signed               | Octave
ASemi      "A semi"        0 24   12   int -12 st signed               | Semitones
AFine      "A fine"        0 1000 500  lin -100 100 ct 0               | Fine tune
ALevel     "A level"       0 1000 1000 pct                             | Level
APan       "A pan"         0 1000 500  bip                             | Pan
AUnison    "A unison"      1 16   1    int 0                           | Unison voices
ADetune    "A detune"      0 1000 447  pow 0 100 2 ct 1                | The outermost unison voices sit this far either side of the note
ASpread    "A spread"      0 1000 700  pct                             | Stereo spread of the unison voices
APhase     "A phase"       0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase
ARandom    "A random"      0 1000 1000 pct                             | How much of a random phase each voice starts with
AWarp1     "A warp 1"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | First warp: how the cycle is read (FM, PM, AM and Ring take the modulator)
AWarp1Amt  "A warp 1 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | First warp's amount
AWarp2     "A warp 2"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | Second warp, after the first
AWarp2Amt  "A warp 2 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Second warp's amount
AMod       "A modulator"   0 4    1    enum Osc_A Osc_B Osc_C Sub Noise | What FM, PM, AM and Ring take (not the slot itself)
AToF2      "A → filter 2"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)

group Osc B
BType      "B engine"      0 5    0    enum Off Wavetable Analog Sample Granular Harmonic | What slot B plays: a morphing wavetable, an analog wave, a sample, grains of a sample, or additive partials (samples, grains and partials take no warps)
BTable     "B table"       0 10   2    enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User | Wavetable (User: a table loaded for this slot)
BPos       "B position"    0 1000 0  pct                             | Position in the table (frames morph smoothly)
BOct       "B octave"      0 8    4    int -4 oct signed               | Octave
BSemi      "B semi"        0 24   12   int -12 st signed               | Semitones
BFine      "B fine"        0 1000 500  lin -100 100 ct 0               | Fine tune
BLevel     "B level"       0 1000 1000 pct                             | Level
BPan       "B pan"         0 1000 500  bip                             | Pan
BUnison    "B unison"      1 16   1    int 0                           | Unison voices
BDetune    "B detune"      0 1000 447  pow 0 100 2 ct 1                | The outermost unison voices sit this far either side of the note
BSpread    "B spread"      0 1000 700  pct                             | Stereo spread of the unison voices
BPhase     "B phase"       0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase
BRandom    "B random"      0 1000 1000 pct                             | How much of a random phase each voice starts with
BWarp1     "B warp 1"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | First warp: how the cycle is read (FM, PM, AM and Ring take the modulator)
BWarp1Amt  "B warp 1 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | First warp's amount
BWarp2     "B warp 2"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | Second warp, after the first
BWarp2Amt  "B warp 2 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Second warp's amount
BMod       "B modulator"   0 4    0    enum Osc_A Osc_B Osc_C Sub Noise | What FM, PM, AM and Ring take (not the slot itself)
BToF2      "B → filter 2"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)

group Osc C
CType      "C engine"      0 5    0    enum Off Wavetable Analog Sample Granular Harmonic | What slot C plays: a morphing wavetable, an analog wave, a sample, grains of a sample, or additive partials (samples, grains and partials take no warps)
CTable     "C table"       0 10   3    enum Basic PWM Harmonics Formants Sync_sweep FM_sweep Organ Resonant Digital Grit User | Wavetable (User: a table loaded for this slot)
CPos       "C position"    0 1000 0  pct                             | Position in the table (frames morph smoothly)
COct       "C octave"      0 8    4    int -4 oct signed               | Octave
CSemi      "C semi"        0 24   12   int -12 st signed               | Semitones
CFine      "C fine"        0 1000 500  lin -100 100 ct 0               | Fine tune
CLevel     "C level"       0 1000 1000 pct                             | Level
CPan       "C pan"         0 1000 500  bip                             | Pan
CUnison    "C unison"      1 16   1    int 0                           | Unison voices
CDetune    "C detune"      0 1000 447  pow 0 100 2 ct 1                | The outermost unison voices sit this far either side of the note
CSpread    "C spread"      0 1000 700  pct                             | Stereo spread of the unison voices
CPhase     "C phase"       0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase
CRandom    "C random"      0 1000 1000 pct                             | How much of a random phase each voice starts with
CWarp1     "C warp 1"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | First warp: how the cycle is read (FM, PM, AM and Ring take the modulator)
CWarp1Amt  "C warp 1 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | First warp's amount
CWarp2     "C warp 2"      0 11   0    enum None Bend+ Bend− Squeeze Mirror Asym Sync Window_sync FM PM AM Ring | Second warp, after the first
CWarp2Amt  "C warp 2 amt"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Second warp's amount
CMod       "C modulator"   0 4    0    enum Osc_A Osc_B Osc_C Sub Noise | What FM, PM, AM and Ring take (not the slot itself)
CToF2      "C → filter 2"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)

group Sub
SubShape    "Sub shape"     0 3    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square   | Sub oscillator wave
SubOct      "Sub octave"    0 2    1    enum 0 -1 -2                    | Octaves from the note
SubLevel    "Sub level"     0 1000 0    pct                             | Sub level
SubPan      "Sub pan"       0 1000 500  bip                             | Sub pan
SubToF2     "Sub → filter 2" 0 1000 0   pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)

group Noise
NoiseColor  "Noise color"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | 0 %: dark (lowpassed from 100 Hz); 100 %: white
NoiseLevel  "Noise level"   0 1000 0    pct                             | Noise level
NoisePan    "Noise pan"     0 1000 500  bip                             | Noise pan
NoiseToF2   "Noise → filter 2" 0 1000 0 pct                             | Balance between filter 1 (0 %) and filter 2 (100 %)

group Filter 1
F1Type      "F1 type"       0 12   1    enum Off Ladder_24 Ladder_12 LP_12 LP_24 BP_12 BP_24 HP_12 HP_24 Notch Peak Comb+ Comb− | Filter model (Comb: the cutoff is its pitch)
F1Cutoff    "F1 cutoff"     0 1000 750  freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
F1Reso      "F1 reso"       0 1000 150  pct                             | Resonance (comb: feedback)
F1Drive     "F1 drive"      0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                   | Drive into the filter
F1Env       "F1 env"        0 1000 600  lin -6 6 oct 1                  | Filter envelope amount
F1Key       "F1 key track"  0 1000 500  pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard (100 %: an octave per octave)
F1Vel       "F1 vel"        0 1000 250  lin 0 4 oct 1                   | Softer notes close the filter by up to this

group Filter 2
F2Type      "F2 type"       0 12   0    enum Off Ladder_24 Ladder_12 LP_12 LP_24 BP_12 BP_24 HP_12 HP_24 Notch Peak Comb+ Comb− | Filter model (Comb: the cutoff is its pitch)
F2Cutoff    "F2 cutoff"     0 1000 750  freq 20 20000                   | Cutoff
F2Reso      "F2 reso"       0 1000 150  pct                             | Resonance (comb: feedback)
F2Drive     "F2 drive"      0 1000 0    lin 0 24 dB 1                   | Drive into the filter
F2Env       "F2 env"        0 1000 500  lin -6 6 oct 1                  | Filter envelope amount
F2Key       "F2 key track"  0 1000 500  pct                             | Cutoff follows the keyboard (100 %: an octave per octave)
F2Vel       "F2 vel"        0 1000 0  lin 0 4 oct 1                   | Softer notes close the filter by up to this
Routing     "Filter routing" 0 1000 0   pct                             | 0 %: filter 1 into filter 2 (serial); 100 %: side by side (parallel)

group Amp env
AmpA        "Amp attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
AmpD        "Amp decay"     0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
AmpS        "Amp sustain"   0 1000 800  pct                             | Sustain level
AmpR        "Amp release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time

group Filter env
FltA        "Flt attack"    0 1000 100  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
FltD        "Flt decay"     0 1000 520  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
FltS        "Flt sustain"   0 1000 300  pct                             | Sustain level
FltR        "Flt release"   0 1000 450  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time

# P1b (appended): the Analog engine's parameters for each slot.
group Osc A
AShape     "A shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
APw        "A pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
ADrift     "A drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are
group Osc B
BShape     "B shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
BPw        "B pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
BDrift     "B drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are
group Osc C
CShape     "C shape"       0 4    2    enum Sine Triangle Saw Square Pulse | The Analog engine's wave
CPw        "C pulse width" 0 1000 1000 lin 3 50 % 1                   | The Analog engine's pulse width (Pulse)
CDrift     "C drift"       0 1000 200  pct                             | The Analog engine's voices each a little out of tune (up to ±12 cents), as analog oscillators are

# P1b (appended): modulation. Two DAHDSR envelopes with curves, four LFOs, four macros and sixteen
# routes (source, destination, amount), evaluated per note on the control grid.
group Mod env 1
E1Delay    "Env1 delay"    0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Delay before the attack
E1A        "Env1 attack"   0 1000 300  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
E1Hold     "Env1 hold"     0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Hold at the top
E1D        "Env1 decay"    0 1000 600  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
E1S        "Env1 sustain"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
E1R        "Env1 release"  0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
E1ACurve   "Env1 att curve" 0 1000 500 bip                             | Attack shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E1DCurve   "Env1 dec curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Decay shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E1RCurve   "Env1 rel curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Release shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E1Sync     "Env1 sync"     0 1    0    switch Seconds Beats            | Beats: each time is read as beats of the song's tempo (1 s = 1 beat)
group Mod env 2
E2Delay    "Env2 delay"    0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Delay before the attack
E2A        "Env2 attack"   0 1000 300  time 0.0005 20                  | Attack time
E2Hold     "Env2 hold"     0 1000 0    pow 0 10 3 s 3                  | Hold at the top
E2D        "Env2 decay"    0 1000 600  time 0.0005 20                  | Decay time
E2S        "Env2 sustain"  0 1000 0    pct                             | Sustain level
E2R        "Env2 release"  0 1000 500  time 0.0005 20                  | Release time
E2ACurve   "Env2 att curve" 0 1000 500 bip                             | Attack shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E2DCurve   "Env2 dec curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Decay shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E2RCurve   "Env2 rel curve" 0 1000 200 bip                             | Release shape: −100 % fast start, 0 straight, +100 % slow start
E2Sync     "Env2 sync"     0 1    0    switch Seconds Beats            | Beats: each time is read as beats of the song's tempo (1 s = 1 beat)
group LFO 1
L1Shape    "LFO1 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
L1Rate     "LFO1 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
L1Sync     "LFO1 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
L1Retrig   "LFO1 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
L1Phase    "LFO1 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
L1Fade     "LFO1 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
group LFO 2
L2Shape    "LFO2 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
L2Rate     "LFO2 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
L2Sync     "LFO2 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
L2Retrig   "LFO2 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
L2Phase    "LFO2 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
L2Fade     "LFO2 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
group LFO 3
L3Shape    "LFO3 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
L3Rate     "LFO3 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
L3Sync     "LFO3 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
L3Retrig   "LFO3 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
L3Phase    "LFO3 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
L3Fade     "LFO3 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
group LFO 4
L4Shape    "LFO4 shape"    0 7    0    enum Sine Triangle Saw_up Saw_down Square S&H Smooth Drawn | Waveform (Drawn: the LFO's own breakpoints, drawn in the editor)
L4Rate     "LFO4 rate"     0 1000 500  freq 0.02 50                    | Rate (free)
L4Sync     "LFO4 sync"     0 11   0    enum Free 1/32 1/16T 1/16 1/8T 1/8 1/4T 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | Tempo sync (overrides the rate)
L4Retrig   "LFO4 retrig"   0 1    1    switch                          | Restart with each note (one per note); off: one free LFO for all notes
L4Phase    "LFO4 phase"    0 1000 0    lin 0 360 ° 0                   | Start phase (retrig)
L4Fade     "LFO4 fade"     0 1000 0    pow 0 5 2 s 2                   | Fade-in time after the note starts
group Macros
M1       "Macro 1"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
M2       "Macro 2"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
M3       "Macro 3"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
M4       "Macro 4"       0 1000 0    pct                             | A knob for routes to follow
group Routes
R1Src      "R1 source"     0 17   0    enum Off Mod_env_1 Mod_env_2 LFO_1 LFO_2 LFO_3 LFO_4 Amp_env Filter_env Velocity Key Mod_wheel Aftertouch Macro_1 Macro_2 Macro_3 Macro_4 Random | Route 1: what modulates
