# P2 (appended): the Sample and Granular engines' parameters for each slot. "position" (above) is the
# sample's start (Sample) or the centre grains are taken from (Granular); tuning, level, pan, unison,
# detune and spread are the slot's own. Samples and grains take no warps.
group Osc A
ASmpSrc    "A sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
ASmpRoot   "A root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
ASmpLoop   "A loop"        0 2    0    enum Off Forward Ping_pong      | Sample engine: how the sample loops while a note is held (Off: plays once)
ASmpLoopStart "A loop start" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop starts, as a share of the sample
ASmpLoopEnd "A loop end"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop ends, as a share of the sample
ASmpFade   "A loop fade"    0 1000 0    lin 0 500 ms 0                  | Sample engine: how long the loop's end fades into its start (0: a hard wrap, right for loops of whole periods; raise it when the loop points are not)
ASmpRev    "A reverse"     0 1    0    switch                          | Sample engine: plays the sample backwards
AGrSize    "A grain size"  0 1000 500  time 0.005 0.5                  | Granular engine: length of each grain
AGrRate    "A grain rate"  0 1000 700  freq 1 100                      | Granular engine: grains started per second (a little uneven, as grains in a cloud are)
AGrSpray   "A spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
AGrScan    "A scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
AGrJitter  "A grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
AGrShape   "A grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
AGrRev     "A grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
AGrWidth   "A grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field
group Osc B
BSmpSrc    "B sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
BSmpRoot   "B root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
BSmpLoop   "B loop"        0 2    0    enum Off Forward Ping_pong      | Sample engine: how the sample loops while a note is held (Off: plays once)
BSmpLoopStart "B loop start" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop starts, as a share of the sample
BSmpLoopEnd "B loop end"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop ends, as a share of the sample
BSmpFade   "B loop fade"    0 1000 0    lin 0 500 ms 0                  | Sample engine: how long the loop's end fades into its start (0: a hard wrap, right for loops of whole periods; raise it when the loop points are not)
BSmpRev    "B reverse"     0 1    0    switch                          | Sample engine: plays the sample backwards
BGrSize    "B grain size"  0 1000 500  time 0.005 0.5                  | Granular engine: length of each grain
BGrRate    "B grain rate"  0 1000 700  freq 1 100                      | Granular engine: grains started per second (a little uneven, as grains in a cloud are)
BGrSpray   "B spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
BGrScan    "B scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
BGrJitter  "B grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
BGrShape   "B grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
BGrRev     "B grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
BGrWidth   "B grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field
group Osc C
CSmpSrc    "C sample"      0 5    0    enum Choir Strings Bell Pluck Texture User | The sample the Sample and Granular engines play (built-in ones are made by code; User: one loaded for this slot)
CSmpRoot   "C root"        0 127  60   int 0                           | The note the sample sounds at its own pitch (MIDI note, 60 = C4)
CSmpLoop   "C loop"        0 2    0    enum Off Forward Ping_pong      | Sample engine: how the sample loops while a note is held (Off: plays once)
CSmpLoopStart "C loop start" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop starts, as a share of the sample
CSmpLoopEnd "C loop end"   0 1000 1000 pct                             | Sample engine: where the loop ends, as a share of the sample
CSmpFade   "C loop fade"    0 1000 0    lin 0 500 ms 0                  | Sample engine: how long the loop's end fades into its start (0: a hard wrap, right for loops of whole periods; raise it when the loop points are not)
CSmpRev    "C reverse"     0 1    0    switch                          | Sample engine: plays the sample backwards
CGrSize    "C grain size"  0 1000 500  time 0.005 0.5                  | Granular engine: length of each grain
CGrRate    "C grain rate"  0 1000 700  freq 1 100                      | Granular engine: grains started per second (a little uneven, as grains in a cloud are)
CGrSpray   "C spray"       0 1000 100  pct                             | Granular engine: how far from the centre grains may start (100%: anywhere in the sample)
CGrScan    "C scan"        0 1000 500  lin -2 2 × 2                    | Granular engine: how fast the centre moves through the sample (1×: its own speed, 0: frozen, negative: backwards)
CGrJitter  "C grain pitch" 0 1000 0    pow 0 1200 2 ct 0               | Granular engine: how far each grain's pitch may wander from the note
CGrShape   "C grain shape" 0 4    0    enum Hann Triangle Tukey Gauss Percussive | Granular engine: the window every grain fades in and out with
CGrRev     "C grain reverse" 0 1000 0  pct                             | Granular engine: the share of grains that play backwards
CGrWidth   "C grain width" 0 1000 500  pct                             | Granular engine: how far grains scatter across the stereo field

# P3a (appended): the Harmonic engine's parameters for each slot. "position" (above) morphs from the first set to the
# second; tuning, level, pan, unison, detune, spread and phase are the slot's own. Partials take no warps.
group Osc A
AHSet     "A harmonics"  0 13   0    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the first set of partial levels (made by code; User: the first frame of the slot's loaded wavetable, analysed)
AHSet2    "A harmonics 2" 0 13  1    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the second set, which "position" morphs to (User: the last frame of the slot's loaded wavetable)
AHPartials "A partials"  1 128  32   int 0                           | Harmonic engine: how many partials sound (those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes anyway); each added partial costs CPU
AHTilt    "A tilt"      0 1000 500  lin -24 24 dB 1                 | Harmonic engine: brightness; each octave of partials louder (+) or softer (−) by this many dB on top of the set (loudness stays)
AHOddEven "A odd even"  0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: + weakens the even partials (towards a hollow, odd-only tone), − weakens the odd ones (towards the octave above)
AHStretch "A stretch"   0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the pitch: + stretches them apart (bells, glass, plucked wire), − bunches them (clusters)
AHDamp    "A damp"      0 1000 0    pct                             | Harmonic engine: how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held (0: they last; 100%: a pluck)
group Osc B
BHSet     "B harmonics"  0 13   0    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the first set of partial levels (made by code; User: the first frame of the slot's loaded wavetable, analysed)
BHSet2    "B harmonics 2" 0 13  1    enum Saw Square Triangle Organ Reed Brass Strings Vowel_A Vowel_O Bright Comb Random Octaves User | Harmonic engine: the second set, which "position" morphs to (User: the last frame of the slot's loaded wavetable)
BHPartials "B partials"  1 128  32   int 0                           | Harmonic engine: how many partials sound (those above the Nyquist limit are dropped on high notes anyway); each added partial costs CPU
BHTilt    "B tilt"      0 1000 500  lin -24 24 dB 1                 | Harmonic engine: brightness; each octave of partials louder (+) or softer (−) by this many dB on top of the set (loudness stays)
BHOddEven "B odd even"  0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: + weakens the even partials (towards a hollow, odd-only tone), − weakens the odd ones (towards the octave above)
BHStretch "B stretch"   0 1000 500  lin -100 100 % 0                | Harmonic engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the pitch: + stretches them apart (bells, glass, plucked wire), − bunches them (clusters)
BHDamp    "B damp"      0 1000 0    pct                             | Harmonic engine: how fast the upper partials die away while a note is held (0: they last; 100%: a pluck)
